nd Three-Dimensional Sectional Anatomy With MRI</source><publisher-loc>Vienna, Austria</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Springer-Verlag</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-Schmahmann5"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmahmann</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyon</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Toga</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Petrides</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><source>MRI Atlas of the Human Cerebellum</source><publisher-loc>San Diego</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Academic Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-Dimitrova1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dimitrova</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Weber</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Redies</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kindsvater</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Maschke</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>MRI atlas of the human cerebellar nuclei.</article-title><source>Neuroimage</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>240</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12482081</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-VanEssen1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Essen</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Surface-based atlases of cerebellar cortex in the human, macaque, and mouse.</article-title><source>Ann N Y Acad Sci</source><volume>978</volume><fpage>468</fpage><lpage>479</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12582074</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-Jansen1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jansen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Brodal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1940</year><article-title>Experimental studies on the intrinsic fibres of the cerebellum. II. The cortico-nuclear projection.</article-title><source>J Comp Neurol</source><volume>73</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>321</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-Jansen2"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jansen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Brodal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1942</year><article-title>Experimental studies on the intrinsic fibres of the cerebellum. III. The cortico-nuclear projection in the rabbit and the monkey (Macacus rhesus).</article-title><source>Norske Vid Akad, Avh I, Math Nat KI</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-Snider1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Snider</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Eldred</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>1952</year><article-title>Cerebrocerebellar relationships in the monkey.</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14908622</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005101-Chambers1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chambers</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Sprague</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1955</year><article-title>Functional localization in the cerebellum. I. Organization in longi